# Independent portable calculation review

Result: **11/11 independent probe groups passed** against frozen patch
`69a5fa55efbf961bb2760bffec4edfdc16ee6df575a84045961fe4e9ee5bbb45`.
No blocking finding remains from this bounded code and runtime review.

The actual implementation, shared adapter, current full adapter, installed SDK
and ephemeris were bundled in memory with esbuild and executed under Node
22.23.2. No calculator or receipt mock replaced those functions. `identities.json`
records all four frozen source hashes, the patch and candidate archive hashes,
the actual loaded module paths/hashes, and the harness/bundle identities. Source
hashes were checked before and after the run. Some installed dependency paths
resolve through the scratch checkout's links to the root checkout; their actual
paths and bytes are recorded. The archive was hashed; this probe does not itself
repeat the separate full installed-package-to-archive member comparison.

The independent cases cover historical year 0099, state isolation between
calculations, fixed errors for revoked context proxies, frozen snapshots without
Date objects, exact once-only input property reads, accessor rejection without
invocation, detachment from mutable chart/input/context branches, requested versus
actual polar houses, unknown time with explicit source spelling, preserved full
adapter input identity and reference semantics, and missing-location/noon defaults.
Raw results are in `probe.log` and `result.json`; `probe.mjs` is the executable
harness. All data is synthetic. No product file or user storage was edited.

The review identified one wording boundary, now documented and regression-tested
in the frozen source: context is captured **after calculation**, so a caller-owned
input getter can change context before capture. The independent timing case
confirms this behavior and subsequent detachment. The function does not promise
an atomic entry-time snapshot or authenticate provenance claims. No duplicate
context validator or same-realm sandbox was added.

The shared mapper retains existing `full.ts` input identity and angle/house/aspect
references. Its body and flag projections remain fresh arrays. The portable path
uses receipt-derived canonical input and freezes the detached receipt/snapshot,
while its presentation chart remains mutable. `Readonly<NatalEnvelope>` provides
shallow compile-time protection and remains compatible with the SDK serializer;
recursive immutability is enforced at runtime. This review does not claim deep
compile-time readonly SDK arrays.

To reproduce with the same checkout, author evidence and installed dependencies:

```sh
/private/tmp/zodiacs-platform-runtime/node_modules/node/bin/node /private/tmp/zodiacs-platform-portable-review/probe.mjs /private/tmp/zodiacs-platform-portable-calculation /private/tmp/zodiacs-platform-portable-evidence > /private/tmp/zodiacs-platform-portable-review/probe.log 2>&1
```

The harness writes only beside itself. Reproduction requires the frozen author's
`source.patch` and `identity.json`; it fails before running cases on mismatched
source or patch bytes. Output timestamps change on a rerun.

This is independent agent review and finite Node execution evidence. It is not
human approval, broad astronomical/historical certification, browser verification,
account migration acceptance, publication, deployment or external adoption.
